  "gradient descent learning rate step size learning rate schedule stochastic gradient descent sgd mini batch momentum adam convergence local minimum optimisation epochs",
  "Gradient descent trains models by repeatedly nudging the parameters in the direction that reduces the loss most quickly.",
  "The gradient is the vector of partial derivatives of the loss with respect to each parameter, pointing uphill; each step moves parameters a small amount against it. The learning rate sets the step size: too large and training diverges or oscillates, too small and it crawls. Batch gradient descent uses all data for each step, stochastic gradient descent (SGD) uses one example, and mini-batch uses small batches, the usual choice. Momentum and adaptive optimisers like Adam speed up and stabilise training. Feature scaling helps it converge, and an epoch is one full pass through the data.",
